# Vercel deployment hygiene.
#
# vercel.json rewrites are filesystem-first: every file that ships is
# publicly fetchable at its repo path AND adds to the deployment.
# Only the Django runtime (api/, app dirs with their templates/,
# static/ and prompts/ trees, industry_analyser/, committed
# frontend_dist/, manage.py, requirements.txt, pyproject.toml,
# uv.lock, wsgi.py) is needed at runtime. Cross-check against
# INSTALLED_APPS before adding exclusions — app dirs must keep
# shipping their templates/ and static/ trees.

# Docs, planning, agent config — `**` so app-level docs also stay
# out (fetcher/README.md, blogs/BLOG_SCRAPER_CALLSTACK.md, …);
# rewrites are filesystem-first so shipped files are publicly served
**/*.md
docs/
openspec/
vision/
.devin/
.agents/
.claude/
.vscode/

# Infra, CI and the Cloud Run path — shell/terraform sources are
# matched at any depth so they stay covered if a dir-level exclusion
# above is ever narrowed
terraform/
.github/
Dockerfile
cloudbuild.yaml
*.sh
*.tf
*.tfvars
*.tfstate*

# Local state and secrets — must never ship or be fetchable
.env*
private_settings.json
ca.pem
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
db.sqlite3
db_backups/
logs/
venv/
.vercel/

# Gitignored local configs — absent in CI checkouts, but keep them
# out of a `vercel deploy` CLI upload's public surface. `config.yaml`
# is name-matched at any depth so future app configs stay covered.
fetcher/config.json
fetcher/config_v2.json
fetcher/config.template.json
config.yaml

# Lint/deploy metadata Vercel doesn't already filter out (it never
# serves .env*, .gitignore, .dockerignore or .vercelignore itself)
.flake8
.gcloudignore

# Local collectstatic output — Vercel has no build step, so a stale
# staticfiles/ would mask the committed frontend_dist/ assets
staticfiles/

# SPA sources and node_modules never ship — Vercel runs no build
# step for this project (no buildCommand in vercel.json, and
# [tool.vercel.scripts] needs framework detection we don't get), so
# only the committed frontend_dist/ build output is needed.
# Shipping frontend/ would also expose the TS sources publicly —
# rewrites are filesystem-first.
frontend/
node_modules/

# Tests and Python artifacts
tests/
tests.py
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# One-off maintenance/job scripts (management commands live inside
# the app packages and are never invoked on Vercel)
scripts/
